{"parentUuid":"2a52da55-9c86-4264-ab7b-cf9938057154","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01U9MWg3BYTfQAjNFLn5LoVS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LbPSDM5p52Lno9QbEuJVVK","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"drat-trim LRAT verified checker performance comparison 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8168,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":349,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8168},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8168,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caotg1VVAaJvcLwvZM5nk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2128ef8-ce1a-4bbb-ac3c-8facc04d29cf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:07.427Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4666dce1-1645-470b-941a-32c073eef67b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X4CsqoQ9mjuHGGpDKbWe8S","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT Competition 2024 2025 LRAT proof verification mandatory dual checker\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/output.html\"},{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-63498-7_26\"},{\"title\":\"Trusted Scalable SAT Solving with on-the-fly LRAT Checking\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-sat-trusted-pre.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Trusted Scalable SAT Solving with On-The-Fly LRAT Checking\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.25\"},{\"title\":\"Trusted Scalable SAT Solving with On-The-Fly LRAT Checking\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2024-sat-trusted.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Automated Reasoning (2025) 69:12\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10817-025-09725-w.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satisfiability.org/SAT24/\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/rules.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about LRAT proof verification in the SAT Competition 2024 and 2025. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## LRAT Proof Verification in SAT Competition\n\nUNSAT certificates (proofs) are required for the Main track of the SAT Competition. The search results show that proof logging & checking matured over the last decade.\n\n## Verified Proof Checkers\n\nSeveral verified LRAT and LPR proof checking tools are presented, including cake_lpr by Yong Kiam Tan, Marijn J. H. Heule, and Magnus O. Myreen, and GRAT: a formally verified (UN)SAT proof checker by Peter Lammich.\n\n## On-the-Fly LRAT Checking\n\nRecent developments in SAT Competition have focused on on-the-fly proof verification. Recent advances have enabled powerful distributed SAT solvers to emit proofs of unsatisfiability, which renders them as trustworthy as sequential solvers. However, this mode of operation is still lacking behind conventional distributed solving in terms of scalability.\n\nRegarding the specific mention of \"mandatory dual checker\" in your query - I could not find explicit information about this specific requirement in the search results. The results focus on proof verification and checking mechanisms but don't detail a mandatory dual checker system for the 2024-2025 competitions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b06ce975-0349-4bc4-ad80-13cc620c3887","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:12.201Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4666dce1-1645-470b-941a-32c073eef67b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f79e667d-1cb0-4baa-85cc-d8a0f05a7282","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EG49hTzo3Be515W9D2p7Wv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LIDRUP IDRUP incremental SAT proof format CaDiCaL 2.x 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cadical/NEWS.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying Incremental SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/FazekasPollittFleuryBiere-LPAR24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying Incremental SAT Solving Katalin Fazekas 1, Florian Pollitt\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/papers/FazekasPollittFleuryBiere-LPAR24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cadical: Simplified SAT solver | Man Page | Commands | cadical | ManKier\",\"url\":\"https://www.mankier.com/1/cadical\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/releases\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/src/proof.cpp at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/src/proof.cpp\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/lidrup-check\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/lidrup-check\"},{\"title\":\"Proofs for Incremental SAT with Inprocessing Benjamin Kiesl-Reiter\",\"url\":\"https://assets.amazon.science/0f/27/487a4cb24557b9a5d8d4613af264/proofs-for-incremental-sat-with-inprocessing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying Incremental SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/talks/lpar2024_talk.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Revisiting DRUP-based Interpolants with CaDiCaL 2.0 Basel Khouri\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.02608\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about LIDRUP, IDRUP, incremental SAT proof formats, and CaDiCaL:\n\n## Overview\n\nLIDRUP builds on IDRUP as LRAT extends DRAT. Both are incremental proof formats for SAT solving.\n\n## Key Differences Between LIDRUP and IDRUP\n\nCompared to the IDRUP format LIDRUP requires clause identifiers for input and lemma lines and hints in form of antecedent clause identifier lists for lemmas and unsatisfiable core lines. Additionally, LIDRUP format has a unique identifier for each clause explicitly introduced, learned clauses and cores are annotated with clause identifier antecedent chain hints of resolution steps and batched restore, delete and weaken steps.\n\n## CaDiCaL 2.x Support\n\nCaDiCaL added support to generate incremental proofs (LIDRUP) while using IPASIR-UP. Recent versions of CaDiCaL have further improvements: LIDRUP proofs now include information about queries that returned with UNKNOWN result.\n\n## Practical Advantages\n\nThe proof verification process is considerably faster for LIDRUP due to the simplified nature of checking all operations. The IDs provide a simple way to identify clauses and focusing resolution on the antecedent clauses is much faster than propagation through reverse unit propagation.\n\n## Checking Tool\n\nCaDiCaL can produce an IDRUP or LIDRUP certificate recording every interaction and reasoning step it performs. This certificate is then forwarded to Lidrup-Check to verify its correctness.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e00cee64-9c2d-4216-9ce4-5cc36d5c4f31","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:13.215Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f79e667d-1cb0-4baa-85cc-d8a0f05a7282","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2a52da55-9c86-4264-ab7b-cf9938057154","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NuDF1NAxFZFDMSUTnXSXya","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cake_lpr verified LRAT checker CakeML HOL4 performance benchmark 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - tanyongkiam/cake_lpr: LPR proof checking with CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tanyongkiam/cake_lpr\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in ...\",\"url\":\"https://cakeml.org/tacas21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7984575/\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-72013-1_12\"},{\"title\":\"The verified CakeML compiler backend | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/330851837_The_verified_CakeML_compiler_backend\"},{\"title\":\"Verified LRAT and LPR Proof Checking with cake_lpr Yong Kiam Tan\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/cakelpr.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://research.chalmers.se/en/publication/531575\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/cake_lpr:-Verified-Propagation-Redundancy-Checking-Tan-Heule/a23f1afd3c101e136f810e2ceb74dad295aa2b6f\"},{\"title\":\"Verified Propagation Redundancy and Compositional UNSAT Checking in CakeML - International Journal on Software Tools for Technology Transfer\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10009-022-00690-y\"},{\"title\":\"Verified Proof Checking\",\"url\":\"https://cakeml.org/checkers.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about cake_lpr:\n\n## Overview\n\ncake_lpr is a verified LPR proof checker developed in CakeML that represents the first approach to formally verify PR proofs on a succinct representation. The LPR format is backwards compatible with the existing LRAT format, but extends the latter with support for the addition of PR clauses.\n\n## Verification and Implementation\n\nHOL4 is a proof assistant implementing classical higher-order logic, and CakeML is a programming language deeply embedded in HOL4, with its abstract syntax represented as a HOL datatype and its semantics formalized within HOL4. The cake_lpr tool is an efficient verified LPR proof checker with correctness guarantees.\n\n## Recent Performance Improvements (2024-2025)\n\nAs of February 16, 2025, cake_lpr performance was improved by around 5-10% and its compiled binary size was reduced by around 20%. Additionally, as of March 11, 2024, cake_lpr now natively supports LRAT/LPR proof files in binary format.\n\n## Performance Benchmarking\n\nLPR provides efficiency gains over existing proof formats, cake_lpr's strong correctness guarantees are obtained without significant sacrifice in its performance, and the compositional proof format enables scalable parallel proof checking for large proofs.\n\n## Real-World Usage\n\ncake_lpr was used to validate the unsatisfiability proofs in the 2020 SAT Competition, and cake_lpr and cake_pb tools are used to audit solver outputs in the annual international SAT solving competitions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5f1dd1f9-3763-4f54-a46e-49207d1857b7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:14.572Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2a52da55-9c86-4264-ab7b-cf9938057154","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f2128ef8-ce1a-4bbb-ac3c-8facc04d29cf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LbPSDM5p52Lno9QbEuJVVK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"drat-trim LRAT verified checker performance comparison 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GRAT -- Efficient Formally Verified SAT Solver Certification Tool Chain\",\"url\":\"https://www21.in.tum.de/~lammich/grat/\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Verified (UN)SAT Certificate Checking | Journal of Automated Reasoning | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10817-019-09525-z\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Verified (UN)SAT Certificate Checking\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/1195523297/34\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - marijnheule/drat-trim: The DRAT-trim proof checker\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marijnheule/drat-trim\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient, Verified Checking of Propositional Proofs⋆\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~mheule/publications/itp17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"drat-trim/lrat-check.c at master · marijnheule/drat-trim\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marijnheule/drat-trim/blob/master/lrat-check.c\"},{\"title\":\"The DRAT format and DRAT-trim checker\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/309317424_The_DRAT_format_and_DRAT-trim_checker\"},{\"title\":\"Submitted by Nils Froleyks Submitted at Institute for Formal Models\",\"url\":\"https://froleyks.de/assets/pdf/Deep%20integration%20of%20SAT%20solving%20and%20model%20checking.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - krobelus/rate: DRAT/DPR proof checker\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/krobelus/rate\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Certified RAT Verification⋆ - UT Computer Science\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.utexas.edu/~marijn/publications/lrat.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about performance comparisons between drat-trim, LRAT, and other verified checkers, though most of the data comes from 2017-2019 rather than specifically 2025. Here's what the research shows:\n\n## Performance Comparison Summary\n\nGRAT is actually faster than the unverified state-of-the-art tool drat-trim, and significantly faster than the verified LRAT tool.\n\n### Verification Time Benchmarks (2017-2018)\n\nTo verify 235 certificates, GRAT required 44 hours, while drat-trim required 72 hours and LRAT required 93 hours. For the certificates by CryptoMiniSAT, which make extensive use of RAT lemmas, the RAT run optimization shows its efficiency: Single-threaded GRAT needs 17h, while drat-trim need 42h and LRAT need 51h.\n\n### Verified vs Unverified Performance\n\nSingle-threaded GRAT is faster than LRAT on every problem. As expected, the difference is more significant on problems that contain RAT lemmas: for the problems that actually contain RAT lemmas, single-threaded GRAT is about 3 times faster than LRAT, while, for the other problems, it is only 1.7 times faster.\n\n### Memory Trade-offs\n\nIn single threaded mode, gratgen needs roughly three times more memory than drat-trim, with eight threads, this figure increases to roughly nine times more memory.\n\n**Note:** The search results don't contain specific 2025 benchmark data. The comparisons shown are primarily from 2017-2019 research papers. For the most current 2025 performance metrics, you may need to check recent SAT competition results or tool releases.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"05223ff0-e1d7-4356-9d17-3077c1de2084","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:15.560Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f2128ef8-ce1a-4bbb-ac3c-8facc04d29cf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
