{"parentUuid":"5b105746-b8ca-4847-bc80-db4d24497a18","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DRRcU6NNF7qywCJ8GotQyj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B3j937jcfHJiN79bwwHxtS","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"AWS firewall verification industrial SAT proof Amazon hardware verification 2024 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5423,"cache_read_input_tokens":21281,"output_tokens":320,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5423},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":320,"cache_read_input_tokens":21281,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5423,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoth6j2uAEtJuouH4L3e","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a1448874-d756-4850-a43b-e36a3e362168","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:21.349Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dfdb15cc-be87-44f9-9c50-7a6d4ebfa2e8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LXDkjUNjyjCH1P21YoQQrj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Carcara Rust SMT proof checker cvc5 alethe 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Carcara: An Efficient Proof Checker and Elaborator for SMT Proofs in the Alethe Format | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-30823-9_19\"},{\"title\":\"Proof format: Alethe — cvc5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.0.0/proofs/output_alethe.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ufmg-smite/carcara\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ufmg-smite/carcara\"},{\"title\":\"Google Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Carcara:+An+Efficient+Proof+Checker+and+Elaborator+for+SMT+Proofs+in+the+Alethe+Format.\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Carcara: An Efficient Proof Checker and Elaborator for SMT Proofs in the Alethe Format\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/370187017_Carcara_An_Efficient_Proof_Checker_and_Elaborator_for_SMT_Proofs_in_the_Alethe_Format\"},{\"title\":\"Overview of the architecture of Carcara. | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Overview-of-the-architecture-of-Carcara_fig1_370187017\"},{\"title\":\"Carcara: An Efficient Proof Checker and Elaborator for SMT Proofs in the Alethe Format | Tools and Algorithms for the Construction and Analysis of Systems\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1007/978-3-031-30823-9_19\"},{\"title\":\"The Alethe Proof Format An Evolving Specification and Reference Haniel Barbosa1\",\"url\":\"https://verit.loria.fr/documentation/alethe-spec.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Invalid Alethe proof produced · Issue #9760 · cvc5/cvc5\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cvc5/cvc5/issues/9760\"},{\"title\":\"Hanna Lachnitt's research works | Stanford University and other places\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Hanna-Lachnitt-2186980237\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Carcara, a Rust SMT proof checker for the Alethe format:\n\n## Overview\n\nCarcara is an independent proof checker and elaborator for Alethe, implemented in Rust. A research paper describing Carcara was published at TACAS 2023.\n\n## Key Features\n\nCarcara is developed in the Rust programming language, and is publicly available under the Apache 2.0 license. It provides both a command line interface and bindings for a Rust API.\n\nAlethe is an established SMT proof format generated by the solvers veriT and cvc5, with reconstruction support in the proof assistants Isabelle/HOL and Coq. Carcara aims to increase the adoption of the format by providing push-button proof-checking for Alethe proofs, focusing on efficiency and usability.\n\n## Architecture and Components\n\nThe main proof checking component contains 6.5k lines of code, while the elaborator has 1k LOC and includes an interface to the cvc5 solver.\n\n## Elaboration Capabilities\n\nAny tool producing detailed Alethe proofs for linear-integer arithmetic reasoning can be used for elaboration, but currently only cvc5 can do so.\n\nThe tool is available on GitHub at https://github.com/ufmg-smite/carcara and represents an important contribution to SMT proof verification infrastructure.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"10b210dd-cb53-462b-bb55-63497acebe6e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:25.751Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dfdb15cc-be87-44f9-9c50-7a6d4ebfa2e8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
