{"parentUuid":"39d58531-268a-4bb7-b51f-74a7eeb6c93f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018NmHyC9DYKPHugtycKSrRW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VeriPB CakePB pseudo-boolean proof 2024 2025 SAT bridge verification\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2025 Markus Anders\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"VERIPB and CAKEPB in the SAT Competition 2023\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2023 Bart Bogaerts\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/downloads/proposals/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Pseudo Boolean Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/\"},{\"title\":\"PB25 Pseudo-Boolean Competition 2025 organized by Olivier Roussel,\",\"url\":\"https://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/slides/PB25.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Certified MaxSAT Preprocessing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-63498-7_24\"},{\"title\":\"Formal Methods in Computer-Aided Design 2024 Translating Pseudo-Boolean Proofs\",\"url\":\"https://repositum.tuwien.at/bitstream/20.500.12708/200790/1/Nukala-2024-Translating%20Pseudo-Boolean%20Proofs%20into%20Boolean%20Clausal%20Proofs-vor.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/output.html\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21\"},{\"title\":\"PBLean: Pseudo-Boolean Proof Certificates for Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.08692v2\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about VeriPB and CakePB for pseudo-boolean proof verification. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## VeriPB and CakePB Overview\n\nVeriPB is a proof checker that accepts proofs in an \"augmented\" proof format with a rich collection of rules for proof logging, while the verified proof checker CakePB only supports a \"kernel\" subset of these commands, with the intended workflow being to use VeriPB as a preprocessor to compile augmented proofs into kernel format for formal checking by CakePB.\n\n## Applications and Development\n\nThe pseudo-Boolean proof format used for VeriPB supports proof logging for decision, enumeration, and optimization problems, as well as problem reformulations, and has been applied to enhanced SAT solving techniques, constraint programming, pseudo-Boolean CDCL-based solving, subgraph solving, presolving in 0-1 integer linear programming, dynamic programming and decision diagrams, and MaxSAT solving.\n\n## 2024-2025 SAT Competition Integration\n\nIn the SAT Competition 2025, the only supported option is to run both VeriPB and CakePB together.\n\nFor the Pseudo-Boolean Competition 2025, the resources allocated to solvers include a 5-hour limit for verification by VeriPB, and certificates of unsatisfiability/optimality must be generated in the VeriPB format.\n\n## Recent Advances (2024-2025)\n\nRecent work has developed an efficient toolchain based on VeriPB and CakePB for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization, moving beyond proof-of-concept works to deliver performance required for real-world deployment.\n\nPBLean provides a method for importing VeriPB pseudo-Boolean proof certificates into Lean 4 using reflection, scaling to proofs with tens of thousands of steps and supporting all VeriPB kernel rules including cutting-plane derivations and redundance-based reasoning.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"11b41400-961c-4903-b99c-1e249bb7576e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:26.558Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"39d58531-268a-4bb7-b51f-74a7eeb6c93f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5b105746-b8ca-4847-bc80-db4d24497a18","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Ch4Uu3Cz6wVSfPuAVqjLa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"GPU accelerated DRAT LRAT proof checking parallel cuDRAT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Certified SAT solving with GPU accelerated inprocessing | Formal Methods in System Design | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10703-023-00432-z\"},{\"title\":\"X-Check: GPU-Accelerated Design Rule Checking via Parallel Sweepline Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://www.cse.cuhk.edu.hk/~byu/papers/C149-ICCAD2022-GPU-DRC.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"X-Check: GPU-Accelerated Design Rule Checking via Parallel Sweepline Algorithms | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10068944\"},{\"title\":\"Complete and Efficient DRAT Proof Checking | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/8602993/\"},{\"title\":\"GPU Accelerated On-the-Fly Reachability Checking | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/7384234/\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-accelerated model checking | Marcin Copik\",\"url\":\"https://mcopik.github.io/projects/prism_gpu/\"},{\"title\":\"DRAT-based Bit-Vector Proofs in CVC4⋆ Alex Ozdemir , Aina Niemetz\",\"url\":\"http://theory.stanford.edu/~barrett/pubs/ONP+19.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Automated Reasoning (2025) 69:12\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10817-025-09725-w.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - marijnheule/drat-trim: The DRAT-trim proof checker\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marijnheule/drat-trim\"},{\"title\":\"Faster LRAT Checking Than Solving with CaDiCaL Florian Pollitt #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.21/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.21.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding GPU-accelerated DRAT/LRAT proof checking and parallel approaches:\n\n## GPU-Accelerated Proof Checking\n\nResearchers have proposed an efficient parallel approach to generate clausal proofs for GPU-accelerated simplifications in DRAT (Deletion Resolution Asymmetric Tautology) format with the goals of creating compact proofs that don't impose overhead to the GPU solver. This work addresses the need to certify SAT solvers using GPU acceleration while maintaining soundness and correctness of unsatisfiability proofs.\n\n## Parallel DRAT and LRAT Checking\n\nAccording to the research, there are not many notable parallel DRAT or LRAT checking approaches currently deployed in practice. However, recent work has focused on improving parallel proof production and checking. Sequential assembly, postprocessing and checking combined succeeded in proof checking that only took 2.1× the solving time, which successfully overcomes the major scalability problems of earlier work.\n\n## LRAT Format Advantages\n\nLRAT proofs include hints to accelerate unit propagation while proof checking. Additionally, LRAT proof checking performed best taking only 30% more time than pure solving, whereas DRAT incurred an overhead of 180% and other approaches required 125% more time than solving.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about \"cuDRAT\" as a specific tool or implementation, but they do show active research in GPU-accelerated SAT proof checking and efforts to make DRAT/LRAT checking more efficient in parallel settings.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f738f557-8290-4017-817f-23f9eff4f288","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:27.484Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5b105746-b8ca-4847-bc80-db4d24497a18","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
