{"parentUuid":"3f09f9b8-7c1a-4e8e-8129-e5190d22e931","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01EpnTNQG1nvTEsTpvLYUrLQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fa1cd2Eh5NLSKEsbkhEBvt","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"cake_lpr\" \"binary format\" LRAT proof checking speed solving overhead 2024"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1263,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4522,"cache_read_input_tokens":26704,"output_tokens":543,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4522},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1263,"output_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":26704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4522,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaothyWEUsSUeHuNr9hJW","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cdeab3e9-5acc-4daa-99c2-8f661168b7f7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:36.186Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9e3f5dc6-ff42-4e37-8fd7-2f20c873ba70","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GctW9iugDmqZf7vbfkdDcR","type":"tool_result","content":"# Linear Incremental DRUP Checker\n\nBased on the GitHub repository, here's what I can tell you:\n\n## What is lidrup-check?\n\nIt's a proof checker for the linear incremental DRUP proof format, written primarily in C (91.4% of the codebase).\n\n## What does it verify?\n\nThe repository description indicates it validates proofs in the DRUP format, though specific technical details about what properties or correctness criteria it checks aren't detailed in the provided content.\n\n## Format & Details\n\nThe acronym \"LIDRUP\" stands for **Linear Incremental DRUP**, suggesting the tool handles proofs with incremental operations in a linear fashion.\n\n## Getting Started\n\nUsers can set up the tool by running `configure && make test` to compile and test the checker.\n\n## Dependencies & Features\n\nThe tool optionally integrates with **CaDiCaL** (a SAT solver). When the configuration script detects CaDiCaL libraries, it compiles `idrup-fuzz`, an additional fuzzing component.\n\n## Other Information\n\n- **Repository stats:** 277 commits, 1 star, MIT license\n- **Language composition:** Primarily C with some C++ and shell scripts\n- **Status:** The repository appears stable with no open issues or pull requests\n\nUnfortunately, the GitHub page doesn't provide performance benchmarks, version numbers, or detailed technical specifications about the DRUP format itself."}]},"uuid":"5c8d693a-b2f7-499b-b98e-fba71ac6dab8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:36.452Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9e3f5dc6-ff42-4e37-8fd7-2f20c873ba70","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6de38b22-6979-4d94-9f4a-907b5b9a862e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016RgLQBnfge4KaZbuREhhRf","type":"tool_result","content":"# CaDiCaL 2.x Releases: Proof Formats and Versions\n\n## Version 2.2.1\nNo specific date provided. Key features:\n- \"New optional stricter API contract checking\" with factor-related validation\n- Deduplication improvements for clause handling\n- Various bug fixes including memory leaks\n\n## Version 2.2.0\nNo specific date provided. Significant developments:\n- **LIDRUP proofs**: \"LIDRUP proofs now include information about queries that returned with UNKNOWN result\" (introduced in 2.1.3, expanded here)\n- ILB interface simplified to use single `ilb` parameter with values 0, 1, or 2\n- Support for shared library compilation\n- New `get_statistic_value` interface\n\n## Version 2.1.3\nNo specific date provided. Notable additions:\n- First introduction of propagation interface supporting assumptions\n- Initial LIDRUP proof capability: solver can now track and report on propagation results\n\n## Version 2.1.2\nNo specific date provided. Technical refinements:\n- IPASIR-UP option improvements\n- Performance regression fixes for incremental solving\n\n## Proof Format Summary\nThe releases mention **LRAT** (from v1.7.0), **DRAT**, **FRAT**, and **LIDRUP** as supported proof formats. LIDRUP appears specific to CaDiCaL's incremental solving with query tracking capabilities."}]},"uuid":"dcddef74-5864-47ed-baec-6629aeeb6334","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:39.168Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6de38b22-6979-4d94-9f4a-907b5b9a862e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3f09f9b8-7c1a-4e8e-8129-e5190d22e931","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A5Ld6a525wqMoj2RgAbGeJ","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your question, but I must be honest: the provided content appears to be a PDF file containing compressed/encoded data that I cannot meaningfully parse. The document shows PDF object streams with FlateDecode compression, but the actual readable text content is not accessible to me in this format.\n\nTo answer your specific questions about SAT Competition 2025 proof verification requirements, checker tools, validation times, file sizes, and dual checker validation, I would need:\n\n1. Plain text or properly decoded content from the competition documentation\n2. Technical specification documents or competition rules\n3. Performance reports or benchmarking data\n\n**I cannot responsibly provide details about proof verification procedures based on this encoded document.** If you have access to the competition's official website, rules document, or a text-based version of this material, I'd be happy to help analyze those sources instead.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 1MB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778188117696-h5aplf.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"58301003-ef9d-4bf7-8667-25ad741c3078","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:41.386Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3f09f9b8-7c1a-4e8e-8129-e5190d22e931","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cdeab3e9-5acc-4daa-99c2-8f661168b7f7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fa1cd2Eh5NLSKEsbkhEBvt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"cake_lpr\" \"binary format\" LRAT proof checking speed solving overhead 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - tanyongkiam/cake_lpr: LPR proof checking with CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tanyongkiam/cake_lpr\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in ...\",\"url\":\"https://cakeml.org/tacas21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7984575/\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Veriﬁed Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML Yong Kiam Tan1(B)\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-030-72013-1_12.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://research.chalmers.se/en/publication/531575\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-72013-1_12\"},{\"title\":\"Verified LRAT and LPR Proof Checking with cake_lpr Yong Kiam Tan\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/cakelpr.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-63498-7_26\"},{\"title\":\"Covering the Last Mile in Trustworthy Automated Reasoning with CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://developer.arm.com/cfs-file/__key/communityserver-blogs-components-weblogfiles/00-00-00-37-98/Yong-Kiam-Tan.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Proof Checking with LRAT in CADICAL (Work in Progress)\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/PollittFleuryBiere-MBMV23.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about cake_lpr, binary format support, and LRAT proof checking:\n\n## Binary Format Support\n\ncake_lpr now natively supports LRAT/LPR proof files in binary format as of March 11, 2024.\n\n## Performance and Proof Checking\n\nUnlike LPR, checking PR proofs via the LRAT route is 5–60x slower than solving those problems, which is a significant drawback to using the route in practice for certifying solver results. However, among LRAT checkers, acl2-lrat is fastest, followed by cake_lpr (LRAT checking), and coq-lrat, although cake_lpr (LRAT checking) is on average 1.3x slower than acl2-lrat.\n\n## Solving Overhead\n\nRegarding the overhead of proof checking compared to solving: The proof format DRAT used in the SAT competition is rather inefficient to check, often even slower to check than it takes the SAT solver to solve the instance and generate the proof. LRAT is much more efficient to check.\n\n## Recent Performance Improvements\n\nAs of February 16, 2025, cake_lpr performance was improved by around 5-10% and its compiled binary size was reduced by around 20%.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d90e0788-a6aa-46ae-b867-dc81d92355bd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:42.316Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cdeab3e9-5acc-4daa-99c2-8f661168b7f7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
