{"parentUuid":"b46d523b-93aa-4103-84aa-ba801b7181fd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WVZgzADPHwRjRieXavbV2G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015ffJWqS4H15a2DmEqu4G7f","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"Schreiber\" trusted scalable SAT MallobSat 2024 LRAT distributed proof"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4439,"cache_read_input_tokens":31226,"output_tokens":334,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4439},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":334,"cache_read_input_tokens":31226,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4439,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4439,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caotj5Cp9vxErHhkiqspy","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e424fa94-46b5-4bb1-9668-bd0f3adf8358","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:52.313Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d0a0d7a0-4727-4151-adf1-e53bf3d4a926","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MG77ThdhLj2cyVTyKwR84P","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT proof file size 70x70 placement CNF encoding gigabytes industrial\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Encodings into SAT Combinatorial Problem Solving (CPS)\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.upc.edu/~erodri/webpage/cps/theory/sat/encodings/slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SATLIB - Benchmark Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~hoos/SATLIB/benchm.html\"},{\"title\":\"Formal Methods in Computer-Aided Design 2023 Verified Encodings for SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://repositum.tuwien.at/bitstream/20.500.12708/188821/1/Codel-2023-Verified%20Encodings%20for%20SAT%20Solvers-vor.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Encoding: An Introduction. As I dug thru material to teach a… | by Venkatesh-Prasad Ranganath | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://rvprasad.medium.com/sat-encoding-an-introduction-44d23049ab2a\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture Notes on SAT Encodings\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~15414/s21/lectures/13-sat-encodings.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluating state-of-the-art # SAT solvers on industrial configuration spaces | Empirical Software Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10664-022-10265-9\"},{\"title\":\"Satisﬁability Suggested Format Last revision: May 8, 1993\",\"url\":\"https://www21.in.tum.de/~lammich/2015_SS_Seminar_SAT/resources/dimacs-cnf.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Solving problems with CNF SAT solvers: The Sudoku example — CS-E3220: Propositional satisfiability and SAT solvers documentation\",\"url\":\"https://users.aalto.fi/~tjunttil/2021-DP-AUT/notes-sat/solving.html\"},{\"title\":\"7. Using SAT Solvers — Logic and Mechanized Reasoning 0.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://avigad.github.io/lamr/using_sat_solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"CNFgen\",\"url\":\"https://massimolauria.net/cnfgen/\"}]\n\nI've performed a web search for your query about SAT proof file size with 70x70 placement CNF encoding in gigabytes for industrial applications. However, the search results returned general information about SAT encoding techniques, benchmark problems, and CNF formats rather than specific information about 70x70 placement problems with gigabyte-sized proofs.\n\nThe results discuss:\n- CNF formulas encoded in DIMACS cnf format\n- How SAT solver performance has evolved from solving formulas with thousands of variables and clauses in the late 1990s to millions of variables and clauses today\n- Various encoding techniques for industrial SAT problems\n\nUnfortunately, the search results do not contain specific information about proof file sizes for 70x70 placement problems or discussions about gigabyte-scale proof files for industrial applications. If you're looking for research on very large proof files or specific industrial placement problem benchmarks, you may want to search for more specialized academic papers or technical reports on SAT proof complexity and industrial applications.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a474946a-c000-4d06-9bd4-eea6464572c7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:56.016Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d0a0d7a0-4727-4151-adf1-e53bf3d4a926","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b8b39420-9529-4508-a1c8-f2df605ad238","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L6oFVyRiY1gXyKBNAhwnkb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Pollitt\" \"Fleury\" \"Biere\" LRAT CaDiCaL on-the-fly checking speed benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Faster LRAT Checking Than Solving with CaDiCaL Florian Pollitt #\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/PollittFleuryBiere-SAT23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Faster LRAT Checking than Solving with CaDiCaL 1 Florian Pollitt # 2\",\"url\":\"https://m-fleury.github.io/ox-hugo/PolittFleuryBiere-SAT2023.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Faster LRAT Checking Than Solving with CaDiCaL - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.21\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Proof Checking with LRAT in CADICAL (Work in Progress)\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/PollittFleuryBiere-MBMV23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Faster LRAT Checking Than Solving with CaDiCaL.\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/sat/PollittFB23.html\"},{\"title\":\"Trusted Scalable SAT Solving with On-The-Fly LRAT Checking\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.25\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27\"},{\"title\":\"Available CAV Evaluation Artifact Reusable CAV Evaluation Artifact CaDiCaL 2.0\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Proof Checking with LRAT in CADICAL (Work in Progress) - Conference papers - VDE Publishing House\",\"url\":\"https://www.vde-verlag.de/proceedings-en/456065009.html\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] CaDiCaL 2.0 | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/CaDiCaL-2.0-Biere-Faller/c0e4581f9af5680b764797c6e5e57ca0c6c3078e\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the work by Pollitt, Fleury, and Biere on LRAT checking with CaDiCaL:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe authors presented an extension to CaDiCaL that generates LRAT natively, along with Lrat-Trim, a tool that trims and checks LRAT proofs in both ASCII and binary format. Their experiments on recent competition benchmarks show that their approach reduces time of proof generation and certification substantially compared to competing approaches using intermediate DRAT or FRAT proofs.\n\n## Key Findings on Speed Benchmarks\n\nThe work shows that LRAT proof checking has a 30% overhead, while FRAT has 125% overhead and DRAT has 180% overhead on top of plain solving without proof generation and checking.\n\nThe DRAT format used in SAT competitions is rather inefficient to check, often even slower to check than it takes the SAT solver to solve the instance and generate the proof. In contrast, LRAT is much easier and way more efficient to check, though much harder to generate.\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nUnlike previous approaches, their implementation generates LRAT directly in the solver without intermediate translations. They further proposed LRAT-Trim, which can trim redundant proof steps from LRAT proofs, which not only reduces proof size but also leads to much faster proof checking.\n\nThe research was published at SAT 2023 and represents a significant advancement in making proof checking practical for SAT solvers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ad1d0a68-0c4e-46dd-bf80-2ee3903223d0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:59.529Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b8b39420-9529-4508-a1c8-f2df605ad238","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b46d523b-93aa-4103-84aa-ba801b7181fd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W9qdjWHHWHY5vLnhx6T6bd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT or-tools UNSAT proof certificate 2024 2025 explanation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"UNSAT Certificates\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2022/certificates.html\"},{\"title\":\"A RESOLUTION-BASED INTERACTIVE PROOF SYSTEM FOR UNSAT PHILIPP CZERNER\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2401.14996\"},{\"title\":\"Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-63498-7_26\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture Notes on SAT & SMT Certificates\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~15414/s23/lectures/20-certificates.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Verified (UN)SAT Certificate Checking | Journal of Automated Reasoning | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10817-019-09525-z\"},{\"title\":\"[2401.14996] A Resolution-Based Interactive Proof System for UNSAT\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.14996\"},{\"title\":\"A Resolution-Based Interactive Proof System for UNSAT\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2401.14996\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/certificates.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/stable/ortools/sat\"},{\"title\":\"A Resolution-Based Interactive Proof System for UNSAT | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-57231-9_6\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's an explanation of UNSAT proof certificates in the context of SAT solvers and optimization tools:\n\n## UNSAT Proof Certificates Overview\n\nModern SAT or QBF solvers are expected to produce correctness certificates. However, certificates have worst-case exponential size (unless NP=coNP), and at recent SAT competitions the largest certificates of unsatisfiability are starting to reach terabyte size.\n\n## Proof Formats\n\nThe most common proof certificate formats are:\n\n1. **RUP (Reverse Unit Propagation)**: RUP certificates contain the clauses learned by the solver. The checker justifies that addition of each clause preserves satisfiability.\n\n2. **DRAT (Delete RUP Augmented with TAuto-reduction)**: The DRAT format is backwards compatible with both the DRUP and RUP formats. The DRUP format extends the RUP format by allowing it to express clause elimination information within the proof format. Emiting proofs in the binary format reduces the size on disk by approximatedly a factor of three compared to the conventional (plain) DRAT format.\n\n## CP-SAT and OR-Tools\n\nOR-Tools includes drat_writer.h which writes UNSAT proof in the DRAT format. This allows to check the correctness of an UNSAT proof with the third party program DRAT-trim.\n\n## Recent Research (2024-2025)\n\nRecent work has explored alternatives to traditional certificates. Couillard et al. have suggested to replace certificates with interactive proof systems based on the IP=PSPACE theorem. The overall running time of the protocol is linear in the time needed by a standard BDD-based algorithm, and the time invested by the verifier is polynomial in the size of the formula.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"df2e1830-d327-4244-8807-3ca05c3eb54e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:00.440Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b46d523b-93aa-4103-84aa-ba801b7181fd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e424fa94-46b5-4bb1-9668-bd0f3adf8358","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aafcddf4215ab99e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ffJWqS4H15a2DmEqu4G7f","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Schreiber\" trusted scalable SAT MallobSat 2024 LRAT distributed proof\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Trusted Scalable SAT Solving with on-the-fly LRAT Checking\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-sat-trusted-pre.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Trusted Scalable SAT Solving with On-The-Fly LRAT Checking\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.25\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat and MallobSat-ImpCheck In the SAT Competition 2024 Dominik Schreiber\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-mallob.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Scalable Trusted SAT Solving with on-the-fly 1 LRAT Checking 2\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-sat-scalable-pre.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27\"},{\"title\":\"Trusted Scalable SAT Solving with On-The-Fly LRAT Checking\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2024-sat-trusted.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - domschrei/mallob: Malleable Load Balancer. Massively Parallel Logic Backend. Award-winning SAT solving for the cloud.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Automated Reasoning (2025) 69:12\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10817-025-09725-w.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat naps in the SAT Competition 2025 Dominik Schreiber\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2025-mallob-naps.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design Dominik Schreiber # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/SchreiberRigiLupertiBiere-SAT25.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the research you're inquiring about. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nRecent advances have enabled powerful distributed SAT solvers to emit proofs of unsatisfiability, which renders them as trustworthy as sequential solvers. However, this mode of operation is still lacking behind conventional distributed solving in terms of scalability. The core limiting factor is the requirement of a single, persistent artifact at the end of solving that is then checked independently (and sequentially). As an alternative, a bottleneck-free setup exploits recent advancements in producing and processing LRAT information to immediately check all solvers' reasoning on-the-fly.\n\n## The IMPCHECK Approach\n\nRather than producing a single persistent proof file and then checking it, each solver's LRAT proof output is checked on-the-fly by a separate checker process without writing it to disk. To transfer the guarantee of a clause's soundness across processes, each checker signs each checked clause with a cryptographic signature (based on 128-bit SIPHASH) which is bundled with the clause during sharing. The receiving checker validates the signature before adding the clause like an original, \"axiomatic\" clause.\n\n## Related Work\n\nMallob and its tightly integrated distributed general-purpose SAT solving engine, MallobSat, received a large amount of attention, including five gold medals in the International SAT Competition's Cloud Track in a row. Mallob is the first distributed system that supports incremental SAT solving and is also the first system transferring proof technology to parallel and distributed SAT solving in a scalable manner.\n\nThe research appears to be centered on the 2024 SAT Competition where this trusted, scalable SAT solving approach with on-the-fly LRAT checking was presented.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"952904dd-ab0b-4408-8561-3b5efad1f354","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:03.648Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e424fa94-46b5-4bb1-9668-bd0f3adf8358","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
